    "site_desc": "Located at the Senda Darwin Biological Station, in a old-growth rainforest. Locally named \"pomponal\"  from the common name of Sphagnum, is an anthropogenic peatland, formed after the forest is cut or a forest fire. The station is 15 km east of Ancud, in the Chiloé Island, close to the Huicha river.",
